  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Use the half-angle formulas to find each of the following:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{8}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt2}}{2}$",
          "worked": "Since $\\frac{\\pi}{8}$ is in Quadrant I, take the positive root.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{8}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\cos(\\pi/4)}{2}}\\\\\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{8}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\sqrt2/2}{2}}\\\\\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{8}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt2}}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{8}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt2-1$",
          "worked": "Since $\\frac{\\pi}{8}$ is in Quadrant I, take the positive root.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{8}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos(\\pi/4)}{1+\\cos(\\pi/4)}}\\\\\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{8}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{2-\\sqrt2}{2+\\sqrt2}}\\\\\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{8}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{(2-\\sqrt2)^2}{2}}\\\\\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{8}&=\\sqrt{(\\sqrt2-1)^2}\\\\\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{8}&=\\sqrt2-1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{12}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt3}}{2}$",
          "worked": "Since $\\frac{\\pi}{12}$ is in Quadrant I, take the positive root.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{12}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos(\\pi/6)}{2}}\\\\\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{12}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\sqrt3/2}{2}}\\\\\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{12}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt3}}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{12}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2-\\sqrt3$",
          "worked": "Since $\\frac{\\pi}{12}$ is in Quadrant I, take the positive root.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{12}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos(\\pi/6)}{1+\\cos(\\pi/6)}}\\\\\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{12}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{2-\\sqrt3}{2+\\sqrt3}}\\\\\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{12}&=\\sqrt{(2-\\sqrt3)^2}\\\\\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{12}&=2-\\sqrt3.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{12}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt3}}{2}$",
          "worked": "Since $\\frac{\\pi}{12}$ is in Quadrant I, take the positive root.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{12}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\cos(\\pi/6)}{2}}\\\\\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{12}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\sqrt3/2}{2}}\\\\\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{12}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt3}}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{24}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt3}}}{2}$\n\nUse the positive half-angle root and the value of $\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{12}$.",
          "worked": "From part (e), $\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{12}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt3}}{2}$. Since $\\frac{\\pi}{24}$ is in Quadrant I, take the positive root.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{24}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos(\\pi/12)}{2}}\\\\\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{24}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt3}/2}{2}}\\\\\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{24}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt3}}}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{16}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt2}}}{2}$\n\nUse the positive half-angle root and the value of $\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{8}$.",
          "worked": "From part (a), $\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{8}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt2}}{2}$. Since $\\frac{\\pi}{16}$ is in Quadrant I, take the positive root.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{16}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\cos(\\pi/8)}{2}}\\\\\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{16}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt2}/2}{2}}\\\\\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{16}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt2}}}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q11-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{16}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt2}}}{2}$\n\nUse the positive half-angle root and the value of $\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{8}$.",
          "worked": "From part (a), $\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{8}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt2}}{2}$. Since $\\frac{\\pi}{16}$ is in Quadrant I, take the positive root.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{16}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos(\\pi/8)}{2}}\\\\\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{16}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt2}/2}{2}}\\\\\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{16}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt2}}}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      }
    ]
